<article class="env-corollary" id="57F0FD">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/57F0FD">Corollary <span data-tag="57F0FD">3.3.1.2</span>.</a> Let $p: X \rightarrow S$ be a Cartesian fibration of simplicial sets, and let $S \rightarrow T$ be a categorical equivalence. Then there exists a Cartesian fibration $Y \rightarrow T$, and an equivalence of $X$ with $S \times _ T Y$ (as Cartesian fibrations over $X$). </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Proposition <a href="/tag/AB6F70" data-tag="AB6F70">3.3.1.1</a> implies that the right derived functor $R p^{\ast }$ is essentially surjective. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>